{"skill":{"slug":"interview-simulator","displayName":"Interview Simulator"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1773498812455,"changelog":"Interview Simulator skill initial release:\n\n- Simulates realistic mock interviews for any role and experience level, adapting to user input.\n- Supports engineering, product, business, operations, people, and admin positions with tailored interview modules.\n- Guides users through configurable interview sessions with clear, professional questioning and adaptive difficulty.\n- Provides constructive feedback, scoring, and improvement suggestions after each answer.\n- Session concludes with a detailed scorecard summary, strengths, areas to improve, and study recommendations.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"README.md","size":5155,"sha256":"72e09233472ad57742fa727268252d25c00a63c24476663376fe019496f5b06f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10570,"sha256":"02f3f0a81577dc8ec91c0d1218ca7bf482ffbe42970305ab742d595415e667ef","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2110,"sha256":"647024b1cac636d530d548228a7f9c243d818f9a5d70e13bfb8f4b0152c573bb","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789176539161,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7f50d04bb52b68bcb6a53746dd7b0b1e5ba5b537279fc05b919dbe01295836e9","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7f50d04bb52b68bcb6a53746dd7b0b1e5ba5b537279fc05b919dbe01295836e9","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086043193},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":23,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789176539161},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a prompt-only mock interview skill with no code execution, persistence, or hidden access, though users should be careful when sharing resume details.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill is pure Markdown and does not request local filesystem access, network access, credentials, tools, APIs, or account mutation authority.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The README instructs users to load a Markdown prompt into an LLM system prompt or custom instruction area; there are no install scripts, dependencies, remote payloads, or executable files.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Activation examples are broad, including interview-prep language and resume/CV prompts, but the resulting behavior remains limited to interview simulation and feedback.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No artifact instructions create persistence, modify memory, install services, alter tools, or retain data beyond the active conversation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifacts consistently describe a universal mock interview simulator that asks questions, role-plays interviews, scores answers, and optionally tailors questions from user-provided resume text.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before using the resume-based flow, remove unnecessary personal information such as phone numbers, addresses, identifiers, and confidential employer details. Consider using a clear phrase like 'mock interview for...' when you want the skill active.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Resume analysis is an optional, user-provided input path that fits targeted interview preparation; the artifact should ideally warn users to redact personal details, but it does not request automatic file access or hidden data collection.\n[SQP-1] expected: The broad preparation examples could make activation less explicit in some hosts, but they still map to interview preparation and do not trigger privileged or destructive behavior.\n[EA3] expected: Supporting many professions is the documented purpose of the skill, not evidence of unrelated agency; the behavior remains question asking, feedback, scoring, and role-play.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789176539161}}}}}